coreUtils
=========

General-purpose infrastructure on which the rest of Pyxplot is built: data
structures, memory management, error reporting and access to the operating
system. Each .c file has a matching .h file declaring its functions and types.

backup.c
    Makes a backup copy (filename~N) of an existing file before Pyxplot
    overwrites it, when the user has turned on "set backup".

dict.c
    The dictionary type: (key, value) pairs kept sorted by key, with a binary
    tree of key hashes for fast lookup. Dictionaries hold variable namespaces,
    the members of modules and user-level dict objects, and many internal
    tables.

errorReport.c
    Reports errors, warnings and informational messages to the user, prefixed
    with the file and line being processed, and writes debugging logs. Errors
    are counted so that Pyxplot can exit with a non-zero status, and a lock lets
    threads report messages safely.

getPasswd.c
    Looks up users' home directories and real names in the password database,
    e.g. to expand filenames such as ~/data.dat.

list.c
    The doubly-linked list type, which holds user-level list objects and any
    internal sequence of items of unknown length.

memAlloc.c
    A pool allocator with nested, numbered contexts. Short-lived memory, such
    as the results of parsing a command, is allocated in a context and freed
    all at once when Pyxplot has finished with it.

stringList.c
    Splits strings into lists of words, for the help command.
